  "description": "The Maniac Latin Disciples (MLD) are a predominantly Hispanic, multi-racial Folk Nation street gang founded in approximately 1966 in Humboldt Park, Chicago, originating as a Puerto Rican baseball club known as the Latin Scorpions. The gang was founded by Albert 'Hitler' Hernandez, who was stabbed to death by two Latin Kings in 1972 at age 18, sparking a lasting rivalry with the Latin Kings. Estimated at 7,500–10,000 members, the MLD have expanded to Ohio, the Quad Cities, Boston, Wisconsin, Michigan, Indiana, Tennessee, Texas, New York, and Florida.",
